text:p.text:span:
X*,
M* = arg minX, M ∑ᵢ,j ρ( ‖ zᵢⱼ - h(xᵢ, mⱼ) ‖_Σ_ij²
)

office:text.text:p:
where h(xᵢ, mⱼ) is the projection
function of point mⱼ onto pose xᵢ, and ρ(·) is a robust function (e.g.,
Huber) [2], [4].

H6: Predictive risk modeling
reduces collisions. The primary endpoint is collisions per kilometer;
near misses and minimum clearance are secondary outcomes.
